course: dictionary
lesson: 16075
title: Wakeful and the many faces of awake
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Wakeful is one of them. Read the sentence around it to find which meaning fits. «I had a wakeful night, staring at the ceiling and listening to the rain.» Here wakeful means you could not sleep.
explain: The second meaning is watchful and alert. «The wakeful guard noticed the tiny noise by the gate.» The guard is not sleepy at all. He is ready and paying close attention.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does «I had a not-able-to-sleep night» still make sense? Yes, so you have the right meaning. Does «The alert guard noticed the noise» still make sense? Yes, so alert is a good synonym here.
fact: Wakeful is an adjective, so it describes a noun: «a wakeful night» describes the night.
fact: «Wakeful» means not able to sleep, or awake when you would normally sleep.
fact: «Wakeful» can also mean watchful and alert, ready to notice things around you.
fact: The ending -ful means full of, so wakeful is like full of being awake.
fact: Awake and alert are close in meaning, but wakeful is often used in stories and formal writing, such as «a wakeful night».
exercise: «I had a wakeful night, and I kept looking at the clock.» What does wakeful mean here? | *Not able to sleep | Sleepy and yawning all day | Noisy and loud | Fast asleep in bed
exercise: «The wakeful guard watched the gate all night.» Which word means nearly the same as wakeful here? | Lazy | Dozy | *Alert | Sleepy
exercise: Mia says screens before bed can make children wakeful. What does she mean? | Children get hungry at night | Children like to dance at school | Children want to sleep all day | *Children find it hard to fall asleep
test: «Grandma was wakeful all night, listening to the wind.» What does wakeful mean? | Happy and singing | Tired and fast asleep | *Awake and not able to sleep | Hungry for breakfast
test: Which word is the opposite of wakeful? | Lively | Alert | *Drowsy | Watchful
exam: «The wakeful nurse checked on the baby every hour, ready for the smallest cry.» What does wakeful suggest here? | Bored and lazy | *Watchful and alert | Sleeping soundly | Cold and hungry
